{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":492530,"name":"G0uv4","username":"g0uv4","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/g0uv4/{size}/116397_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T09:23:30.266Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492530-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492530-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492530-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492530-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Windows, the default shortcut to open Settings is Ctrl+,. For Traditional Chinese (Taiwan) users, Ctrl+, is the normal way many IMEs insert the full-width comma character 「，」. Pressing Ctrl+, while typing therefore opens Settings instead of inserting the comma, which makes composing Chinese text in the app painful.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492530-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492530-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot desktop on Windows.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFocus a chat input (or any text field).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSwitch to a Traditional Chinese IME (e.g. Microsoft Bopomofo / Zhuyin).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePress Ctrl+, intending to type the full-width comma 「，」.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eObserve: Settings opens; the comma is not inserted.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492530-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492530-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCtrl+, should insert 「，」 when used via the IME / as the user’s punctuation chord. Opening Settings should use a shortcut that does not collide with CJK IME punctuation on Windows (or Settings should not fire during IME composition).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492530-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492530-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492530-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492530-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot desktop (Windows)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492530-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492530-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is a keyboard shortcut / IME conflict, distinct from the stuck-Ctrl Settings bug discussed in \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/problemas-with-hot-keys-on-grok-bot-desktop/168998\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eProblemas with hot keys on Grok Bot desktop\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492530-suggested-fix-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492530-suggested-fix-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSuggested fix\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChange the Windows/Linux default Open Settings shortcut away from Ctrl+, (e.g. Ctrl+Shift+, or Ctrl+Alt+,). Keep Cmd+, on macOS if desired.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIgnore the Open Settings shortcut while an IME composition session is active in the focused input.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMake the Open Settings shortcut remappable / disableable in Settings, with a conflict hint.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDocument the conflict for Traditional Chinese users.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492530-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492530-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T12:46:18.365Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171839,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-windows-ctrl-settings-shortcut-blocks-traditional-chinese-full-width-comma","display_username":"G0uv4","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/problemas-with-hot-keys-on-grok-bot-desktop/168998","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Problemas with hot keys on Grok Bot desktop","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":131160,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-windows-ctrl-settings-shortcut-blocks-traditional-chinese-full-width-comma/171839/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":492789,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T12:47:43.645Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/g0uv4\"\u003e@g0uv4\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the detailed report.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI was able to trace what you’re describing: when the Bopomofo IME handles Ctrl+, to produce 「，」, Grok Bot still sees the key press as its Settings shortcut and opens Settings instead of letting the IME insert the comma. I’ve flagged this to the team.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the meantime, one way to get 「，」 without hitting the shortcut would be to press Shift+Space to switch the IME to full-width (全形) mode, then press the , key on its own. It inserts 「，」 directly and does not trigger Ctrl+,. Press Shift+Space again to go back to half-width.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCould you confirm the Grok Bot version you’re on (Help → About) and whether this also happens for other Ctrl+punctuation chords from the IME, e.g. Ctrl+. for 「。」? That tells us whether only the Settings shortcut is in the way.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T12:47:43.645Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":1,"readers_count":0,"score":0.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":171839,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-windows-ctrl-settings-shortcut-blocks-traditional-chinese-full-width-comma","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Community Support Engineer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":87436,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-windows-ctrl-settings-shortcut-blocks-traditional-chinese-full-width-comma/171839/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,